{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md | sed -n '350,372p;552,605p'\nnl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md | sed -n '277,310p;411,438p'\ndate -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT'\ndate '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %z (%Z)'\"","aggregated_output":"   350\t`:ffi-call` and has no tail operand.\n   351\t\n   352\tThe pc side table is `{pc {:kind :closure, :params [sym ...], :source e}}`\n   353\tfor every `:closure` pc, with `:params` read from the resolver side table's\n   354\t`:params` by resolved lambda id, and `{pc {:kind :var, :source e}}` for\n   355\tevery load pc. `:source` is the source eid, read through the resolver side\n   356\ttable's `:source` map, never the resolved id, so it matches `lower`'s\n   357\t`:yin.code/source` at the same pc. `adapt` is the composition `lower-stack`\n   358\tafter `resolve` and is the one public entry that takes named datoms to an\n   359\timage.\n   360\t\n   361\tThe lift executes with synthesized names by default: fresh against the\n   362\timage's free-name set and against each other, so no lifted binder can\n   363\tcapture a free name. A supplied pc side table is used only when every\n   364\t`:closure` entry's parameter count equals the instruction's arity, its\n   365\tnames are capture-free by the same rule, and `adapt` of the lifted result\n   366\treproduces the original image byte for byte; otherwise it is discarded and\n   367\tsynthesis is used. This is the rule the B2 box's completion criteria\n   368\talready require; it is stated here as the contract.\n   369\t\n   370\tThis removes the fused design's vector-level scope reconstruction:\n   371\t`closure-body-ranges`, `layout-conforms?`, `body-owner`, `chain-of`, and\n   372\tthe vector-level `resolve-var` and `rewrite`. That machinery existed only\n   552\t### B2: resolver and stack lowerer\n   553\t\n   554\t    New: src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_resolve.cljc\n   555\t    New: test/yin/vm/debruijn_resolve_test.cljc\n   556\t    New: src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linearize.cljc\n   557\t    New: test/yin/vm/debruijn_linearize_test.cljc\n   558\t    Existing edits: none\n   559\t    Must not change: yin.vm.linearize and named lowering semantics\n   560\t\n   561\tB2 is two namespaces (section 3). `yin.vm.debruijn-resolve` owns `resolve`:\n   562\tnamed datoms to resolved tuples plus binder side table, its scope validator,\n   563\tand the inverse `unresolve` used as a test oracle. It is shared with the\n   564\tregister design and depends on nothing in this design below section 3.1.\n   565\t`yin.vm.debruijn-linearize` owns `lower-stack`, `adapt`, `lift`, and the\n   566\tpublic `named-canonical-vector` helper the structural comparison uses. The\n   567\tfused implementation's `closure-body-ranges`, `layout-conforms?`,\n   568\t`body-owner`, `chain-of`, vector-level `resolve-var`, `rewrite`, and the\n   569\tduplicate vector-level `image-scope-defect` are removed, not moved: scope\n   570\tis known on the tree, and B1's validator is the vector-level check.\n   571\t\n   572\tCompletion requires, for the resolver: deterministic output on every host,\n   573\tevery node type resolved or refused with a named diagnostic, exact free\n   574\tnames and scalars, the duplicate-parameter fixture `(fn [x x] x)` resolving\n   575\tto `[0 1]`, out-of-range hand-built resolved tuples refused by\n   576\t`validate-resolved`, a cyclic input refused, the shared-occurrence fixtures\n   577\t(one variable entity under `[x]` and `[y]` resolving bound `[0 0]` and free\n   578\t`x`; the same entity under `[x]` and `[x] [y]` resolving `[0 0]` and\n   579\t`[1 0]`; one entity twice under equal contexts yielding one record\n   580\treferenced twice; one lambda entity under two contexts yielding two\n   581\tresolved lambdas), and `unresolve(resolve x, side-table) = x` as a datom\n   582\tset over the corpus and those fixtures.\n   583\t\n   584\tFor the stack lowerer: deterministic output, every node and opcode, the\n   585\tsection 3.2 structural opcode-by-opcode comparison with `lower` differing\n   586\tonly at variable and closure operands, image encode/validate/load round\n   587\ttrips, and `lift(adapt x, side-table) = canonical-vector(lower x)`. The lift\n   588\tis a function of the image plus its pc side table. With the original binder\n   589\tnames in the side table, equality holds; with synthesized names, the lifted\n   590\tresult is alpha-equivalent to `lower x`, including `(fn [x x] x)`.\n   591\tSynthesized names must be fresh against the image's free-name set. A\n   592\tsupplied side table is accepted only when `adapt` of its lift returns the\n   593\toriginal image. Every image B2 emits must be accepted by B1's validator, and\n   594\tevery hand-built out-of-range image must be rejected by B1's validator. The\n   595\tgolden image bytes and H values frozen in B1 must be reproduced unchanged\n   596\tby `adapt`; the refactor changes derivation, not bytes.\n   597\t\n   598\t### B3: de Bruijn VM kernel\n   599\t\n   600\t    New: src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc\n   601\t    New: test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_test.cljc\n   602\t    Existing edits: none\n   603\t    Must not change: semantic VM, engine, IVM protocols, named environment,\n   604\t    merged projection namespace\n   605\t\n   277\t## 4. Resolved-tuples-to-register lowering\n   278\t\n   279\t### 4.1 Input and validation\n   280\t\n   281\tThe lowerer accepts only resolved tuples from the section 2.1 resolver and\n   282\ttheir side table. It calls the resolver's `validate-resolved` first and\n   283\trefuses on its diagnostic, identically to `lower-stack`, before emitting\n   284\tanything. It does not accept named datoms directly, does not rerun name\n   285\tresolution, and does not accept a stack image. B2 remains the only\n   286\tproducer of `:yin.debruijn.code/*` stack images; this lowerer is the only\n   287\tproducer of `:yin.debruijn.register/*` register images.\n   288\t\n   289\tBecause the input is an expression graph rather than a flat instruction\n   290\tstream, there is no control-flow graph to recover and no abstract operand\n   291\tstack to simulate: every intermediate value is an expression whose extent\n   292\tis known from its record. The walk is the named linearizer's order,\n   293\toperator then operands left to right, lambda bodies out of line in\n   294\tdiscovery order, `if` evaluating one arm, with occurrences expanded\n   295\tpositionally: a resolved record referenced twice is lowered twice, at two\n   296\tplaces, exactly as `lower-stack` and `lower` do. Every body has one\n   297\tenclosing lexical chain by construction, and every bound reference is\n   298\talready validated against it. The lowerer's own checks are register bounds,\n   299\tbody ranges, and target bounds, applied to its output.\n   300\t\n   301\t### 4.2 Register classes\n   302\t\n   303\tEach body has two disjoint register banks:\n   304\t\n   305\t    L0 ... L(n-1)     current body's parameters\n   306\t    T0 ... T(k-1)     expression temporaries\n   307\t\n   308\t`n` is the body's declared arity. `:load-bound rd depth position` reads the\n   309\texisting lexical frame chain and writes `rd`; it does not assign an outer\n   310\tframe's slot a register number in the current body. Thus frame 0 remains the\n   411\t### R1: register dimension and lowerer\n   412\t\n   413\t    New: src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc\n   414\t    New: src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc\n   415\t    New: test/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile_test.cljc\n   416\t    Existing edits: none\n   417\t    Must not change: B1 code, B2 lowerer, B3 VM, resolver contract,\n   418\t    dao.stream protocols\n   419\t\n   420\tImplement the descriptor, validation, deterministic lowering from resolved\n   421\trecords, allocation, encoding, R, and the lift to `:yin.code/*`. Completion\n   422\trequires every resolved node type mapped or refused with a named diagnostic,\n   423\tbyte-identical repeated lowerings, golden register vectors, cross-host R\n   424\tagreement, the section 2.2 address law extended to the register image, and\n   425\tthe lift law `lift(lower-register (resolve x), side-table)` alpha-equivalent\n   426\tto `canonical-vector(lower x)` under the arity and layout caveats of the\n   427\tstack design's B2 box.\n   428\t\n   429\t### R2: effects and stream forms\n   430\t\n   431\t    Existing source: src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc\n   432\t    New: test/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects_test.cljc\n   433\t    Existing edits: none\n   434\t    Must not change: dao.stream, lease, waitset, B0-B3 semantics\n   435\t\n   436\tLower stream, gensym, FFI, park, and resume shapes with explicit registers.\n   437\tCompletion compares effect descriptors and blocked outcomes with the stack\n   438\tpath without executing a register VM.\n2026-09-22 10:37:09 GMT\n2026-09-22 17:37:09 +0700 (+07)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
